@v532 kernel.value.record "collection" "eslm-everyday-source.jsonl" "locator" "dataset.jsonl:60" "sourceId" "RO-006-10" "sourceDigest" "sha256:5a237fa90205b8803cf417d2309b66d597389b93a82ddd256305d47fdbe6176e" "sourceFile" "cases/benchmark_006.md"
@v533 kernel.seq.make
@v534 kernel.seq.make
@v535 kernel.value.record "answer" "The main problem is that **one observation does not justify a universal conclusion**. The premise may be relevant, but it is not sufficient for the stated general conclusion.\n\nTo make the argument stronger, add evidence that directly links the premise to the conclusion: more representative observations, relevant comparisons, tests, or information about the causal mechanism, as appropriate. State the conclusion in proportion to the strength of the evidence rather than extending it beyond that evidence." "requiredConcepts" $v533 "forbiddenClaims" $v534
@v536 kernel.value.record "method" "manual-reviewed" "reviewed" true "note" ""
@v537 kernel.seq.make item "core-only"
@v538 kernel.seq.make item "assigned-train-visible" item "source-category:argument-critique" item "domain:logic" item "length:medium"
@v539 kernel.value.record "expectedMinWords" 68 "expectedMaxWords" 180 "acceptableVariations" "A formal fallacy label is optional; identifying the defective logical relationship is required."
@v540 kernel.value.record "format" "eslm-basic-everyday-eval-case" "id" "everyday-0060" "source" $v532 "pool" "source-development" "category" "argument-critique" "difficulty" "medium" "scoring" "semantic" "prompt" "Analyze the argument: “I used the product once and it did not work; the product never works.”\n\nIn no more than 180 words, state the main logical problem, explain why the conclusion does not follow sufficiently from the premise, and propose what additional information would make the argument stronger." "reference" $v535 "conversion" $v536 "profiles" $v537 "tags" $v538 "constraints" $v539 "reviewNotes" "Source policy: development-visible"
