@v641 kernel.seq.make item "6" item "45" item "5 minutes" item "test"
@v642 kernel.seq.make
@v643 kernel.value.record "answer" "The plan can be:\n\nDay 1: one basic European history concept; 25 minutes of study, 15 minutes of practical exercise, and 5 minutes of review.\nDay 2: one basic European history concept; 25 minutes of study, 15 minutes of practical exercise, and 5 minutes of review.\nDay 3: one basic European history concept; 25 minutes of study, 15 minutes of practical exercise, and 5 minutes of review.\nDay 4: one basic European history concept; 25 minutes of study, 15 minutes of practical exercise, and 5 minutes of review.\nDay 5: one basic European history concept; 25 minutes of study, 15 minutes of practical exercise, and 5 minutes of review.\nDay 6: review and a short test; 30 minutes for the test and correction, 10 minutes to review mistakes, and 5 minutes for conclusions.\n\nKeep notes brief. At the end of each day, record one unclear point and check it at the beginning of the next day. The goal is not to cover the whole field but to build a stable foundation in European history." "requiredConcepts" $v641 "forbiddenClaims" $v642
@v644 kernel.value.record "method" "template-assisted" "reviewed" true "note" ""
@v645 kernel.seq.make item "core-only"
