@v1242 kernel.value.record "format" "eslm-basic-everyday-eval-case" "id" "everyday-0138" "source" $v1234 "pool" "source-development" "category" "title-generation" "difficulty" "easy" "scoring" "semantic" "prompt" "Turn the sentence into a title of no more than eight words: “The museum is launching an exhibition dedicated to urban photography.”" "reference" $v1237 "conversion" $v1238 "profiles" $v1239 "tags" $v1240 "constraints" $v1241 "reviewNotes" "Source policy: development-visible"
@v1243 kernel.value.record "collection" "eslm-everyday-source.jsonl" "locator" "dataset.jsonl:139" "sourceId" "RO-014-09" "sourceDigest" "sha256:05a61edbbfe860a790db221e76952e263f8c0c905e340ff29f533d04acaca120" "sourceFile" "cases/benchmark_014.md"
@v1244 kernel.seq.make item "notifications" item "interface" item "search" item "favorites"
@v1245 kernel.seq.make
@v1246 kernel.value.record "answer" "I would group the feedback into four themes:\n\n1. **Speed and setup:** quick opening and easy initial setup are positive points.\n2. **Interface and accessibility:** the interface is praised as simple, but there is a request for larger text.\n3. **Search and organization:** favorites are appreciated, but old documents are difficult to find.\n4. **Notifications:** notifications are sometimes missing and sometimes duplicated.\n\nThe clear positive aspects are simplicity, speed, setup, and favorites. The recurring problem is notification reliability because two different comments report incorrect behavior in that area.\n\nThis sample does not establish how frequent the problems are across the entire user base." "requiredConcepts" $v1244 "forbiddenClaims" $v1245
@v1247 kernel.value.record "method" "template-assisted" "reviewed" true "note" ""
@v1248 kernel.seq.make item "core-only"
@v1249 kernel.seq.make item "assigned-train-visible" item "source-category:feedback-synthesis" item "domain:text-analysis" item "length:medium"
@v1250 kernel.value.record "expectedMinWords" 100 "expectedMaxWords" 230 "acceptableVariations" "The grouping may use three or four themes, but it must recognize both notification-related problems."
@v1251 kernel.value.record "format" "eslm-basic-everyday-eval-case" "id" "everyday-0139" "source" $v1243 "pool" "source-development" "category" "feedback-synthesis" "difficulty" "medium" "scoring" "semantic" "prompt" "You have the following eight comments about a fictional application:\n1. “It opens quickly.”\n2. “Sometimes I do not receive notifications.”\n3. “The interface is simple.”\n4. “Search has difficulty finding old documents.”\n5. “I like being able to save favorites.”\n6. “I would like larger text.”\n7. “I received two notifications for the same event.”\n8. “Initial setup was easy.”\n\nGroup the feedback into no more than four themes, state what is positive and which problem recurs. Do not invent frequencies beyond the eight comments. Maximum 220 words." "reference" $v1246 "conversion" $v1247 "profiles" $v1248 "tags" $v1249 "constraints" $v1250 "reviewNotes" "Source policy: development-visible"
@v1252 kernel.value.record "collection" "eslm-everyday-source.jsonl" "locator" "dataset.jsonl:140" "sourceId" "RO-014-10" "sourceDigest" "sha256:dc1dbde6fb4452cf18b0f52184ba93024f239fe3252a63054bf41edc3028a84d" "sourceFile" "cases/benchmark_014.md"
