@v2359 kernel.value.record "collection" "eslm-everyday-source.jsonl" "locator" "dataset.jsonl:263" "sourceId" "RO-027-03" "sourceDigest" "sha256:fbc62e72bba357af33156126f4a21ea2a406cc1f4f0b05f9ff44c1957965dc37" "sourceFile" "cases/benchmark_027.md"
@v2360 kernel.seq.make
@v2361 kernel.seq.make
@v2362 kernel.value.record "answer" "The essential difference is this: a summary compresses the main ideas, while a paraphrase restates content while retaining roughly the same information.\n\nA simple example should show that the terms may be related but answer different questions. They should therefore not be used as synonyms, and neither should be inferred automatically from the other without enough information.\n\n**In short:** the two concepts concern a similar subject but describe different properties or roles; a correct explanation begins by separating those roles clearly." "requiredConcepts" $v2360 "forbiddenClaims" $v2361
@v2363 kernel.value.record "method" "manual-reviewed" "reviewed" true "note" ""
