@v3611 kernel.seq.make
@v3612 kernel.seq.make
@v3613 kernel.value.record "answer" "The essential difference is this: the mean is the sum divided by the number of values, while the median is the middle value after sorting.\n\nA simple example should show that the terms may be related but answer different questions. They should therefore not be used as synonyms, and neither should be inferred automatically from the other without enough information.\n\n**In short:** the two concepts concern a similar subject but describe different properties or roles; a correct explanation begins by separating those roles clearly." "requiredConcepts" $v3611 "forbiddenClaims" $v3612
@v3614 kernel.value.record "method" "manual-reviewed" "reviewed" true "note" ""
@v3615 kernel.seq.make item "quick-assisted" item "real-kb"
