@v4080 kernel.seq.make
@v4081 kernel.value.record "answer" "The essential difference is this: authentication verifies identity, while authorization determines permissions.\n\nA simple example should show that the terms may be related but answer different questions. They should therefore not be used as synonyms, and neither should be inferred automatically from the other without enough information.\n\n**In short:** the two concepts concern a similar subject but describe different properties or roles; a correct explanation begins by separating those roles clearly." "requiredConcepts" $v4079 "forbiddenClaims" $v4080
