@v4949 kernel.value.record "expectedMinWords" 56 "expectedMaxWords" 150 "acceptableVariations" "Other greetings and closings are acceptable; omitting the deadline or inventing reasons is not."
@v4950 kernel.value.record "format" "eslm-basic-everyday-eval-case" "id" "everyday-0550" "source" $v4942 "pool" "source-development" "category" "email-rewriting" "difficulty" "medium" "scoring" "semantic" "prompt" "Rewrite the message as a professional but not rigid email. Preserve all information and limit the answer to 90–140 words. Do not add reasons or deadlines absent from the text.\n\nRaw message: “Hello. You have not sent the file yet. I need it by Tuesday. Check the figures too, because the last version had two errors. Send it when it is ready.” Answer directly and do not add unrequested information." "reference" $v4945 "conversion" $v4946 "profiles" $v4947 "tags" $v4948 "constraints" $v4949 "reviewNotes" "Source policy: development-visible"
