@v5295 kernel.seq.make
@v5296 kernel.value.record "answer" "The essential difference is this: weather describes short-term conditions, while climate describes long-term patterns.\n\nA simple example should show that the terms may be related but answer different questions. They should therefore not be used as synonyms, and neither should be inferred automatically from the other without enough information.\n\n**In short:** the two concepts concern a similar subject but describe different properties or roles; a correct explanation begins by separating those roles clearly. The time scale is the key distinction." "requiredConcepts" $v5294 "forbiddenClaims" $v5295
@v5297 kernel.value.record "method" "manual-reviewed" "reviewed" true "note" "English wording was reviewed against the source response-length metadata."
@v5298 kernel.seq.make item "quick-assisted" item "real-kb"
@v5299 kernel.seq.make item "assigned-train-visible" item "source-category:educational-explanation" item "domain:learning" item "length:medium"
@v5300 kernel.value.record "expectedMinWords" 77 "expectedMaxWords" 190 "acceptableVariations" "The example may vary; the conceptual distinction must be correct and understandable to a student."
