@v5726 kernel.seq.make
@v5727 kernel.seq.make
@v5728 kernel.value.record "answer" "The essential difference is this: RAM is volatile working memory, while an SSD provides persistent storage.\n\nA simple example should show that the terms may be related but answer different questions. They should therefore not be used as synonyms, and neither should be inferred automatically from the other without enough information.\n\n**In short:** the two concepts concern a similar subject but describe different properties or roles; a correct explanation begins by separating those roles clearly." "requiredConcepts" $v5726 "forbiddenClaims" $v5727
@v5729 kernel.value.record "method" "manual-reviewed" "reviewed" true "note" ""
