@v6275 kernel.seq.make item "notifications" item "interface" item "search" item "favorites"
@v6276 kernel.seq.make
@v6277 kernel.value.record "answer" "I would group the feedback into four themes:\n\n1. **Speed and setup:** quick opening and easy initial setup are positive points.\n2. **Interface and accessibility:** the interface is praised as simple, but there is a request for larger text.\n3. **Search and organization:** favorites are appreciated, but old documents are difficult to find.\n4. **Notifications:** notifications are sometimes missing and sometimes duplicated.\n\nThe clear positive aspects are simplicity, speed, setup, and favorites. The recurring problem is notification reliability because two different comments report incorrect behavior in that area.\n\nThis sample does not establish how frequent the problems are across the entire user base." "requiredConcepts" $v6275 "forbiddenClaims" $v6276
@v6278 kernel.value.record "method" "template-assisted" "reviewed" true "note" ""
@v6279 kernel.seq.make item "core-only"
@v6280 kernel.seq.make item "assigned-train-visible" item "source-category:feedback-synthesis" item "domain:text-analysis" item "length:medium"
@v6281 kernel.value.record "expectedMinWords" 100 "expectedMaxWords" 230 "acceptableVariations" "The grouping may use three or four themes, but it must recognize both notification-related problems."
@v6282 kernel.value.record "format" "eslm-basic-everyday-eval-case" "id" "everyday-0698" "source" $v6274 "pool" "source-development" "category" "feedback-synthesis" "difficulty" "medium" "scoring" "semantic" "prompt" "You have the following eight comments about a fictional application:\n1. “It opens quickly.”\n2. “Sometimes I do not receive notifications.”\n3. “The interface is simple.”\n4. “Search has difficulty finding old documents.”\n5. “I like being able to save favorites.”\n6. “I would like larger text.”\n7. “I received two notifications for the same event.”\n8. “Initial setup was easy.”\n\nGroup the feedback into no more than four themes, state what is positive and which problem recurs. Do not invent frequencies beyond the eight comments. Maximum 220 words. Keep the answer clear and concise." "reference" $v6277 "conversion" $v6278 "profiles" $v6279 "tags" $v6280 "constraints" $v6281 "reviewNotes" "Source policy: development-visible"
@v6283 kernel.value.record "collection" "eslm-everyday-source.jsonl" "locator" "dataset.jsonl:699" "sourceId" "RO-070-09" "sourceDigest" "sha256:2b49c392c359133f763bfa947f7d55b7be061f6df00ed42242c2a653b4228f05" "sourceFile" "cases/benchmark_070.md"
