@v6382 kernel.value.record "collection" "eslm-everyday-source.jsonl" "locator" "dataset.jsonl:710" "sourceId" "RO-071-10" "sourceDigest" "sha256:5898a8de22a2e1b64a7ca9cc0fd5df94c97572713c7995647d3fb3b5c474677f" "sourceFile" "cases/benchmark_071.md"
@v6383 kernel.seq.make item "notifications" item "interface" item "search" item "favorites"
@v6384 kernel.seq.make
@v6385 kernel.value.record "answer" "I would group the feedback into four themes:\n\n1. **Speed and setup:** quick opening and easy initial setup are positive points.\n2. **Interface and accessibility:** the interface is praised as simple, but there is a request for larger text.\n3. **Search and organization:** favorites are appreciated, but old documents are difficult to find.\n4. **Notifications:** notifications are sometimes missing and sometimes duplicated.\n\nThe clear positive aspects are simplicity, speed, setup, and favorites. The recurring problem is notification reliability because two different comments report incorrect behavior in that area.\n\nThis sample does not establish how frequent the problems are across the entire user base." "requiredConcepts" $v6383 "forbiddenClaims" $v6384
@v6386 kernel.value.record "method" "template-assisted" "reviewed" true "note" ""
@v6387 kernel.seq.make item "core-only"
@v6388 kernel.seq.make item "assigned-train-visible" item "source-category:feedback-synthesis" item "domain:text-analysis" item "length:medium"
@v6389 kernel.value.record "expectedMinWords" 100 "expectedMaxWords" 230 "acceptableVariations" "The grouping may use three or four themes, but it must recognize both notification-related problems."
@v6390 kernel.value.record "format" "eslm-basic-everyday-eval-case" "id" "everyday-0710" "source" $v6382 "pool" "source-development" "category" "feedback-synthesis" "difficulty" "medium" "scoring" "semantic" "prompt" "You have the following eight comments about a fictional application:\n1. “It opens quickly.”\n2. “Sometimes I do not receive notifications.”\n3. “The interface is simple.”\n4. “Search has difficulty finding old documents.”\n5. “I like being able to save favorites.”\n6. “I would like larger text.”\n7. “I received two notifications for the same event.”\n8. “Initial setup was easy.”\n\nGroup the feedback into no more than four themes, state what is positive and which problem recurs. Do not invent frequencies beyond the eight comments. Maximum 220 words." "reference" $v6385 "conversion" $v6386 "profiles" $v6387 "tags" $v6388 "constraints" $v6389 "reviewNotes" "Source policy: development-visible"
@v6391 kernel.value.record "collection" "eslm-everyday-source.jsonl" "locator" "dataset.jsonl:711" "sourceId" "RO-072-01" "sourceDigest" "sha256:124ec52ea845ea0daa4fd692f5ceb90964cba883f0c7d332d9ba13867289e47d" "sourceFile" "cases/benchmark_072.md"
@v6392 kernel.seq.make item "5" item "45" item "5 minutes" item "test"
@v6393 kernel.seq.make
@v6394 kernel.value.record "answer" "The plan can be:\n\nDay 1: one basic introductory psychology concept; 25 minutes of study, 15 minutes of practical exercise, and 5 minutes of review.\nDay 2: one basic introductory psychology concept; 25 minutes of study, 15 minutes of practical exercise, and 5 minutes of review.\nDay 3: one basic introductory psychology concept; 25 minutes of study, 15 minutes of practical exercise, and 5 minutes of review.\nDay 4: one basic introductory psychology concept; 25 minutes of study, 15 minutes of practical exercise, and 5 minutes of review.\nDay 5: review and a short test; 30 minutes for the test and correction, 10 minutes to review mistakes, and 5 minutes for conclusions.\n\nKeep notes brief. At the end of each day, record one unclear point and check it at the beginning of the next day. The goal is not to cover the whole field but to build a stable foundation in introductory psychology." "requiredConcepts" $v6392 "forbiddenClaims" $v6393
@v6395 kernel.value.record "method" "template-assisted" "reviewed" true "note" ""
@v6396 kernel.seq.make item "core-only"
@v6397 kernel.seq.make item "assigned-train-visible" item "source-category:study-plan" item "domain:learning" item "length:medium"
@v6398 kernel.value.record "expectedMinWords" 100 "expectedMaxWords" 260 "acceptableVariations" "Daily content may vary; the number of days, time limit, review period, and final test are required."
@v6399 kernel.value.record "format" "eslm-basic-everyday-eval-case" "id" "everyday-0711" "source" $v6391 "pool" "source-development" "category" "study-plan" "difficulty" "medium" "scoring" "semantic" "prompt" "I want a simple study plan for introductory psychology. I have 5 days, with 45 minutes per day. I am a beginner and do not want to cover too much. Each day must have one main objective, one practical activity, and five minutes of review. On the final day I want a short self-assessment test.\n\nMake a short, concrete plan of no more than 250 words." "reference" $v6394 "conversion" $v6395 "profiles" $v6396 "tags" $v6397 "constraints" $v6398 "reviewNotes" "Source policy: development-visible"
