@v6482 kernel.seq.make
@v6483 kernel.seq.make
@v6484 kernel.value.record "answer" "The main problem is that **popularity does not establish safety**. The premise may be relevant, but it is not sufficient for the stated general conclusion.\n\nTo make the argument stronger, add evidence that directly links the premise to the conclusion: more representative observations, relevant comparisons, tests, or information about the causal mechanism, as appropriate. State the conclusion in proportion to the strength of the evidence rather than extending it beyond that evidence." "requiredConcepts" $v6482 "forbiddenClaims" $v6483
@v6485 kernel.value.record "method" "manual-reviewed" "reviewed" true "note" ""
@v6486 kernel.seq.make item "core-only"
@v6487 kernel.seq.make item "assigned-train-visible" item "source-category:argument-critique" item "domain:logic" item "length:medium"
@v6488 kernel.value.record "expectedMinWords" 64 "expectedMaxWords" 180 "acceptableVariations" "A formal fallacy label is optional; identifying the defective logical relationship is required."
@v6489 kernel.value.record "format" "eslm-basic-everyday-eval-case" "id" "everyday-0721" "source" $v6481 "pool" "source-development" "category" "argument-critique" "difficulty" "medium" "scoring" "semantic" "prompt" "Analyze the argument: “The product is popular, so it is safe.”\n\nIn no more than 180 words, state the main logical problem, explain why the conclusion does not follow sufficiently from the premise, and propose what additional information would make the argument stronger." "reference" $v6484 "conversion" $v6485 "profiles" $v6486 "tags" $v6487 "constraints" $v6488 "reviewNotes" "Source policy: development-visible"
