@v7154 kernel.value.record "expectedMinWords" 56 "expectedMaxWords" 150 "acceptableVariations" "Other greetings and closings are acceptable; omitting the deadline or inventing reasons is not."
@v7155 kernel.value.record "format" "eslm-basic-everyday-eval-case" "id" "everyday-0795" "source" $v7147 "pool" "source-development" "category" "email-rewriting" "difficulty" "medium" "scoring" "semantic" "prompt" "Rewrite the message as a professional but not rigid email. Preserve all information and limit the answer to 90–140 words. Do not add reasons or deadlines absent from the text.\n\nRaw message: “Hello. You have not sent the file yet. I need it by Thursday. Check the figures too, because the last version had two errors. Send it when it is ready.”" "reference" $v7150 "conversion" $v7151 "profiles" $v7152 "tags" $v7153 "constraints" $v7154 "reviewNotes" "Source policy: development-visible"
