@v8234 kernel.value.record "expectedMinWords" 255 "expectedMaxWords" 850 "acceptableVariations" "The answer may vary but must follow every constraint, use the supplied data, and not invent material information."
@v8235 kernel.value.record "format" "eslm-basic-everyday-eval-case" "id" "everyday-0915" "source" $v8227 "pool" "source-development" "category" "complex-everyday-task" "difficulty" "medium-hard" "scoring" "semantic" "prompt" "Three managers are discussing introducing one meeting-free day per week. A says it would help uninterrupted work but worries that emergencies would be delayed. B supports the idea if there are exceptions for incidents and important clients, but does not want every meeting simply moved to the next day. C says one general rule does not fit everyone: support needs daily coordination, while analytics teams would benefit greatly.\n\nWrite a neutral synthesis, identify agreements and disagreements, and propose a four-week pilot. Define no more than four simple metrics. Do not present the pilot as guaranteed to work. Maximum 750 words." "reference" $v8230 "conversion" $v8231 "profiles" $v8232 "tags" $v8233 "constraints" $v8234 "reviewNotes" "Source policy: development-visible"
