@v8327 kernel.seq.make
@v8328 kernel.seq.make
@v8329 kernel.value.record "answer" "**Friday—easy urban day.** Leave in the morning and arrive around noon. After checking in, allow time for lunch and settling in. The afternoon can include a compact central area and one main attraction. Then reserve at least two completely free hours before dinner.\n\n**Saturday—nature without difficult trails.** Choose an area accessible by car with a short, relatively flat trail, or several viewpoints connected by short drives. Plan about two hours of activity before lunch, a long break, and at most one more easy activity. After returning, keep at least two hours free.\n\n**Rain plan.** Replace the trail with a low-walking indoor activity such as a museum, visitor center, or cultural venue. If the weather permits, add a scenic drive with very short stops.\n\n**Sunday—relaxed half-day.** Have a late breakfast, individual free time, and at most one optional activity near the departure point. Leave early enough for an unhurried return.\n\nThe general principle is one main activity and one optional activity per day, so breaks can be extended without disrupting the schedule.\n\nAdapt the template each morning based on energy and weather. If the friend who tires easily needs a longer break, remove the optional activity, not the break. Treat driving as part of the schedule rather than “free” time. A successful itinerary here preserves room for decisions instead of maximizing the number of checked-off sights. Keep the daily two-hour free period even when an optional activity is removed." "requiredConcepts" $v8327 "forbiddenClaims" $v8328
