@v8486 kernel.value.record "expectedMinWords" 238 "expectedMaxWords" 850 "acceptableVariations" "The answer may vary but must follow every constraint, use the supplied data, and not invent material information."
@v8487 kernel.value.record "format" "eslm-basic-everyday-eval-case" "id" "everyday-0943" "source" $v8479 "pool" "source-development" "category" "complex-everyday-task" "difficulty" "medium-hard" "scoring" "semantic" "prompt" "I have the following notes from a project meeting: version 2.1 was supposed to launch on September 18; the main features are ready; tests show an approximately 25% slowdown above 5,000 simultaneous users; the infrastructure team believes cache optimization may help but has not finished testing; two interface issues remain open; the Beta client is asking for the original date; the product team accepts a delay of no more than one week if performance is not resolved; the budget is on track; testing will be repeated Thursday; the final decision is Friday at 13:00; if there is a delay, Beta must be notified the same day.\n\nWrite an executive summary with: status, risks, decisions already made, matters still undecided, and next actions. Do not turn uncertainties into facts. Maximum 650 words." "reference" $v8482 "conversion" $v8483 "profiles" $v8484 "tags" $v8485 "constraints" $v8486 "reviewNotes" "Source policy: development-visible"
