@v8721 kernel.value.record "format" "eslm-basic-everyday-eval-case" "id" "everyday-0969" "source" $v8713 "pool" "source-development" "category" "complex-everyday-task" "difficulty" "medium-hard" "scoring" "semantic" "prompt" "In a five-person team, the tasks are: A takes 6 hours and must finish before B; B takes 4 hours; C takes 8 hours and may start immediately; D takes 3 hours and depends on C; E takes 5 hours and is independent; F takes 2 hours and must be done after B. Each person has about 6 hours per day available for these tasks for five days. A task cannot be split among several people at the same time.\n\nPropose a simple allocation that respects dependencies, verify the total number of hours, and give a backup plan if C takes 4 extra hours. Do not attempt sophisticated optimization. Maximum 700 words." "reference" $v8716 "conversion" $v8717 "profiles" $v8718 "tags" $v8719 "constraints" $v8720 "reviewNotes" "Source policy: development-visible"
@v8722 kernel.value.record "collection" "eslm-everyday-source.jsonl" "locator" "dataset.jsonl:970" "sourceId" "RO-097-10" "sourceDigest" "sha256:ddddb7ce04902c43546111ede263401f7de180d8208605dfe1996f59d47ef725" "sourceFile" "cases/benchmark_097.md"
