@v8749 kernel.value.record "collection" "eslm-everyday-source.jsonl" "locator" "dataset.jsonl:973" "sourceId" "RO-098-03" "sourceDigest" "sha256:b924e7d31cb5431a26646c2d64b1de761fee75784b187196582f3c0e4c16aa4b" "sourceFile" "cases/benchmark_098.md"
@v8750 kernel.seq.make
@v8751 kernel.seq.make
@v8752 kernel.value.record "answer" "**Week 1—basic statistics.** Reinforce mean, median, mode, range, and elementary measures of variation. Alternate formula review with exercises that require choosing the appropriate measure, not merely calculating it. Final check: 12–15 exercises without notes.\n\n**Week 2—probability.** Begin with events, possible outcomes, simple probabilities, and complements. Use small problems involving coins, dice, and selections. Final check: about 10 problems, including several that require explaining the method.\n\n**Week 3—graphs and integration.** Combine statistics and probability exercises with graph interpretation. Deliberately practice truncated axes, different scales, and misleading comparisons. Final check: a mini-test covering all three sections.\n\n**Week 4—practice exams.** Review recurring errors on the first two days. Take a short practice exam on day 3. On day 4, correct and redo missed problems. Take the second practice exam on day 5.\n\nTrack errors in a four-column table: problem, error type, reason, rule to remember. If the same category appears three times, make it a priority in the next session.\n\nThe plan leaves weekends free and uses the daily 60 minutes for reinforcement rather than excessive coverage.\n\nAt the end of each week, do not track only the total score. Record conceptual, calculation, and question-reading mistakes separately. If the score rises but the same error category remains, adjust the plan. Do not introduce new chapters in the final week; practice exams and error correction take priority. Use the same error table throughout all four weeks." "requiredConcepts" $v8750 "forbiddenClaims" $v8751
@v8753 kernel.value.record "method" "manual-reviewed" "reviewed" true "note" "English wording was reviewed against the source response-length metadata."
