@v8757 kernel.value.record "format" "eslm-basic-everyday-eval-case" "id" "everyday-0973" "source" $v8749 "pool" "source-development" "category" "complex-everyday-task" "difficulty" "medium-hard" "scoring" "semantic" "prompt" "I have four weeks to prepare for an introductory exam with three sections: basic statistics, probability, and graph interpretation. I can study five days a week for about 60 minutes a day. In statistics I know the mean and median but forget formulas. I am a beginner in probability. I am comfortable with graphs but make mistakes when axes are truncated or two graphs use different scales.\n\nI want a four-week plan. Each week must have an objective, exercise types, and an end-of-week check. I want two short practice exams in the final week. Do not recommend specific online resources or assume I can study on weekends. Include a simple method for tracking recurring mistakes. Maximum 750 words." "reference" $v8752 "conversion" $v8753 "profiles" $v8754 "tags" $v8755 "constraints" $v8756 "reviewNotes" "Source policy: development-visible"
