@v8865 kernel.value.record "format" "eslm-basic-everyday-eval-case" "id" "everyday-0985" "source" $v8857 "pool" "source-development" "category" "extraction" "difficulty" "easy" "scoring" "semantic" "prompt" "From the text “Paul Georgescu is 23 years old and lives in Sibiu.” extract the full name and age." "reference" $v8860 "conversion" $v8861 "profiles" $v8862 "tags" $v8863 "constraints" $v8864 "reviewNotes" "Source policy: development-visible"
@v8866 kernel.value.record "collection" "eslm-everyday-source.jsonl" "locator" "dataset.jsonl:986" "sourceId" "RO-099-06" "sourceDigest" "sha256:ac18fd6f306c5d06c785ad403a6442c56adeb6f03d25cc6846bd0980e7a088d0" "sourceFile" "cases/benchmark_099.md"
@v8867 kernel.seq.make
@v8868 kernel.seq.make
@v8869 kernel.value.record "answer" "**A** fits comfortably within the budget and includes the basic equipment, but involves almost 50 minutes of round-trip travel and leaves lunch to be arranged separately. We do not know how well it supports small-group work.\n\n**B** is the least expensive and logistically simple, but has a flaw directly tied to the objective: the room is comfortable for 14 people, not 18. Crowding would reduce the comfort that was identified as the priority.\n\n**C** costs RON 2,600, so it remains under budget. It includes the room, projector, coffee, and lunch and is only 10 minutes from the office. From the supplied data, it minimizes logistics and avoids B’s clear capacity problem.\n\n**Recommendation: C.** The cost is higher but within the limit, while the dominant criteria are comfort and simple organization.\n\n**Backup: A.** If C is unavailable, A is preferable to B because it has no explicit capacity problem and remains under budget. Its layout for group work and lunch arrangements should be clarified. Lunch cost cannot be estimated without more data.\n\nBefore booking, one further check is critical: C’s actual room configuration for small-group work. The data say services are included but do not describe table layout. If C cannot support grouping participants, the recommendation might change. Make the same check for A if it becomes the backup. Comfort and logistical simplicity remain the governing criteria." "requiredConcepts" $v8867 "forbiddenClaims" $v8868
@v8870 kernel.value.record "method" "manual-reviewed" "reviewed" true "note" "English wording was reviewed against the source response-length metadata."
@v8871 kernel.seq.make item "core-only"
@v8872 kernel.seq.make item "assigned-train-visible" item "source-category:complex-everyday-task" item "domain:decision-and-synthesis" item "length:long"
