@v8874 kernel.value.record "format" "eslm-basic-everyday-eval-case" "id" "everyday-0986" "source" $v8866 "pool" "source-development" "category" "complex-everyday-task" "difficulty" "medium-hard" "scoring" "semantic" "prompt" "I have three options for a one-day training session with 18 people. A: external room, RON 1,800 total, includes a projector and coffee but not lunch; 25 minutes of travel each way. B: our room, direct cost RON 0, but comfortable for only 14 people and crowded with extra chairs. C: training center, RON 2,600 total, includes the room, projector, coffee, and lunch; 10 minutes from the office.\n\nThe maximum budget is RON 3,000. The main goal is for people to work comfortably in small groups. Cost matters but is not the dominant criterion. I do not want to organize too many separate things on the day of the event.\n\nCompare the options by comfort, logistics, cost, and fit with the goal. Recommend one and name a backup. Do not invent the lunch price for A. Maximum 700 words." "reference" $v8869 "conversion" $v8870 "profiles" $v8871 "tags" $v8872 "constraints" $v8873 "reviewNotes" "Source policy: development-visible"
@v8875 kernel.value.record "collection" "eslm-everyday-source.jsonl" "locator" "dataset.jsonl:987" "sourceId" "RO-099-07" "sourceDigest" "sha256:5b2253e8f4daf264d5004218588ecf4d2845849aa259f0d946e00cdad000c15e" "sourceFile" "cases/benchmark_099.md"
